{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Purpose Layer of Play.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Purpose Layer of Play.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"purpose layer of play purpose layer of play","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Purpose Layer of Play.md","fileName":"Purpose Layer of Play.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Purpose Layer of Play","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-21 00:27\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Player Experience Layers]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Player Experience Layers","gamesdesignandplay.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Purpose Layer of Play.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Purpose Layer of Play.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"purpose layer of play purpose layer of play","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Purpose Layer of Play.md","fileName":"Purpose Layer of Play.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Purpose Layer of Play","heading":"Purpose Layer of Play","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The purpose layer answers why a player is participating. The purpose may be to win, explore, socialize, perform, master a skill, encounter an authored experience, or pursue a self-created goal.\n\nPurpose organizes the other experience layers by determining which signals, facts, and actions matter. A designer can propose a purpose through goals and framing, but players may adopt another purpose that the game's possibility space permits.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Player Experience Layers","gamesdesignandplay.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Purpose Layer of Play.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Purpose Layer of Play.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"purpose layer of play purpose layer of play","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Purpose L